sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/hygromorph-bilayer-scaling--claude-opus-5-5--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Literature-extracted test of curvature and h^2/D response time across species" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/hygromorph-bilayer-scaling> ;
    dct:description "Extend the repo's pre-registered pine-cone curvature test to the full acceptance criterion using published data only. For each specimen or specimen class in pine cone scales (Reyssat and Mahadevan 2009; Quan et al. 2021; Eger et al. 2022; Dawson et al. 1997), wheat awns (Elbaum et al. 2007), chiral seed pods (Armon et al. 2011) and fabricated bilayers (paper-polymer in Reyssat and Mahadevan; Erb et al. 2013; Gladman et al. 2016; Le Duigou and Castro 2016), extract layer thicknesses, moduli, free swelling strains, diffusivity or permeability, measured curvature change and response time. Predict curvature with the Lean-checked Timoshenko formula (bilayerCurvature_ofEquilibrium) and response time with tau = h^2/D (diffusiveTime_scale). Pass: |log(kappa_measured/kappa_pred)| <= log 1.5 in most specimens; response time slope on log h equals 2 within plus or minus 0.4 among fabricated bilayers of at least three thicknesses." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Per-specimen curvature ratio distribution and response-time exponent with CI, against the pre-registered tolerances." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Fewer than 20 specimens with all inputs independently measured (most papers fit swelling strain from curvature, which is circular); response time series with fewer than three thicknesses." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Pre-register tolerances, extraction rules (only inputs measured independently of the curvature itself; no back-fitted swelling strains) and the specimen count required (20 specimens, five species, or the fabricated-bilayer alternative). 2. Extract from text, tables and digitized figures (with digitization error recorded). 3. Compute predictions and residuals; report per species. 4. Fit log tau on log h for fabricated series with a mixed model by study; report slope and CI. 5. Classify deviations by suspected cause (fibre angle, gradient, viscoelasticity) for approach 2." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Independent per-specimen moduli, swelling strains and diffusivity are rarely reported together; no humidity chamber or printer to measure new specimens." ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:note "Tool: literature-extraction" ;
    skos:note "Tool: figure-digitization" ;
    skos:note "Tool: python" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch10-01> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2009.0184> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actbio.2021.04.049> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.202200458> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/37745> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140097> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1203874> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms2666> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/nmat4544> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep18105> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/hygromorph-bilayer-scaling> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Do real hygromorphs follow bilayer curvature and diffusive response-time scaling?" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2009.0184> dct:title "Hygromorphs: from pine cones to biomimetic bilayers" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Reyssat and Mahadevan 2009, Hygromorphs: from pine cones to biomimetic bilayers" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actbio.2021.04.049> dct:title "Hydration-induced reversible deformation of the pine cone" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Quan et al. 2021, Hydration-induced reversible deformation of the pine cone" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.202200458> dct:title "The Structural and Mechanical Basis for Passive‐Hydraulic Pine Cone Actuation" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Eger et al. 2022, The structural and mechanical basis for passive-hydraulic pine cone actuation" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/37745> dct:title "How pine cones open" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Dawson, Vincent and Rocca 1997, How pine cones open" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140097> dct:title "The Role of Wheat Awns in the Seed Dispersal Unit" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Elbaum et al. 2007, The role of wheat awns in the seed dispersal unit" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1203874> dct:title "Geometry and Mechanics in the Opening of Chiral Seed Pods" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Armon et al. 2011, Geometry and mechanics in the opening of chiral seed pods" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms2666> dct:title "Self-shaping composites with programmable bioinspired microstructures" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Erb et al. 2013, Self-shaping composites with programmable bioinspired microstructures" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/nmat4544> dct:title "Biomimetic 4D printing" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gladman et al. 2016, Biomimetic 4D printing" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep18105> dct:title "Evaluation of force generation mechanisms in natural, passive hydraulic actuators" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Le Duigou and Castro 2016, Evaluation of force generation mechanisms in natural, passive hydraulic actuators" .
}

